Game-Merrills

Nine Men's Morris, also called Merrills, Merels and Mill, as a reusable engine
with a terminal game on top. Two players, nine men each, and a board of three
squares joined at the middle of their sides: place the men, move them along the
lines, and take an enemy man each time three of yours stand in a row.

INSTALLATION

To install this module, run the following commands:

	perl Makefile.PL
	make
	make test
	make install

SUPPORT AND DOCUMENTATION

After installing, you can find documentation for this module with the
perldoc command.

    perldoc Game::Merrills

You can also look for information at:

    RT, CPAN's request tracker (report bugs here)
        https://rt.cpan.org/NoAuth/Bugs.html?Dist=Game-Merrills

    Search CPAN
        https://metacpan.org/release/Game-Merrills


